              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pereō, perīre — \"to perish, to die; to be lost\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In illō incendiō multī periērunt. Many died in that fire."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pereō, perīre, periī, peritum, like eō (taught). In comedy a slave cries periī!, 'I am done for!'"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pereō is built on eō, \"to go\", with per-, here \"to destruction\" (Lewis & Short): to go to ruin. English perish comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
