              "text": "custōs, custōdis — \"a guard, a keeper\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Custōdēs portae dormiēbant, et fūr intrāvit. The guards of the gate were asleep, and the thief got in."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine or feminine, 3rd declension. A satirist asked who would guard the guards themselves. English custody is of its family."
            }
          ]
        },
